    "title": "Fractions",
    "standard": {
        "explanation": "<h3>Unlocking Fractions</h3><p>Fractions are just parts of a whole thing. Like slices of a pizza!</p><div class=\"concept-grid\"><div class=\"concept-card\"><h4><i class=\"fas fa-chart-pie\"></i> Part of a Whole</h4><p>A fraction tells us how many pieces we have out of the total pieces.</p><div class=\"example-box\">1/2 means <strong>1 part</strong> out of <strong>2 total parts</strong>.</div></div><div class=\"concept-card\"><h4><i class=\"fas fa-arrow-up\"></i> Numerator (North)</h4><p>The top number. It shows how many parts we <strong>have</strong>.</p><div class=\"example-box\">In 3/4, <strong>3</strong> is the Numerator.</div></div><div class=\"concept-card\"><h4><i class=\"fas fa-arrow-down\"></i> Denominator (Down)</h4><p>The bottom number. It shows the <strong>total</strong> equal parts.</p><div class=\"example-box\">In 3/4, <strong>4</strong> is the Denominator.</div></div></div><h3>Types of Fractions</h3><div class=\"concept-grid\"><div class=\"concept-card\"><h4><i class=\"fas fa-check\"></i> Proper Fractions</h4><p>Top is smaller than Bottom. It is less than 1.</p><div class=\"example-box\">1/2, 3/4, 7/10</div></div><div class=\"concept-card\"><h4><i class=\"fas fa-exclamation-circle\"></i> Improper Fractions</h4><p>Top is bigger than Bottom. It is more than 1.</p><div class=\"example-box\">5/4, 7/2, 10/3</div></div><div class=\"concept-card\"><h4><i class=\"fas fa-layer-group\"></i> Mixed Numbers</h4><p>A Whole number mixed with a Fraction.</p><div class=\"example-box\">1 1/2 (One and a half)</div></div></div>",
